{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>וְאַנִי הִנְנִי מְחַזֵּק</b> etc. Through HaShem's compassion upon them, He intended to inform them beforehand, lest they be frightened when they see that the sea remained split before the Egyptians just as it had been split before them — they might again begin to think thoughts and diminish the faith in their hearts, and say, ״הִנֵּה הֵמָּה עוֹלִים אַחֲרֵינוּ״ (behold, they are coming up after us), and be very afraid. Therefore He informed them and said to them: Know that it was from Me — the matter of making their hearts stubborn, and I am spreading a net for their feet."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:50.490931061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}